/ Stage 10 (decision 67): a typed list holds its element type. The type door can make a closed list<T>, so what
/ goes in is born as a path, not left as text.
Start
- set %files% as list of path = ["a.txt", "b.txt"]
- assert %files!type.name% equals "list"
- assert %files[0]!type.name% equals "path", "each element is born as the list's element type"
